        mountCategory = "Dungeon and Raids",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A rare drop with daily or weekly loot limits can require many repeated clears.\n\n1. At the ground-level Icecrown Citadel raid entrance (53.7, 87.0 in Icecrown), set the legacy raid to 25-player Heroic. Enter the raid itself, not one of the nearby five-player dungeons. Use an unsaved weekly lockout.\n\n2. Clear Marrowgar and Deathwhisper, then start the gunship event. Take a rocket pack if needed, use the cannons, and handle the enemy mage if the cannons freeze. Continue through Deathbringer Saurfang.\n\n3. Clear all three upper branches needed to unlock the Frozen Throne: Festergut, Rotface and Putricide; the Blood Princes and Blood-Queen Lana'thel; then Sindragosa. Use the transporters as they unlock. For this mount-only route, you can pass around Valithria Dreamwalker without healing her.\n\n4. Make sure Putricide's and the other wing-end access requirements are finished, then use the central upper-spire teleporter to the Frozen Throne. Confirm that the Lich King encounter is still 25-player Heroic before telling Tirion to begin.\n\n5. Defeat the Lich King while avoiding Shadow Traps and the platform edge. At his scripted mass-kill ending, remain in the encounter and wait for the resurrection and Tirion's sequence; do not release spirit simply because he killed you. Finish him when attackable again.\n\n6. Loot the Lich King and use Invincible's Reins if they drop. This is a rare weekly chance, not a guaranteed Heroic reward. Return after reset or clear on other eligible characters; a Normal kill or 10-player kill is not a mount attempt.",
