        },
        itemId = 51955,
        name = "Icebound Frostbrood Vanquisher",
        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 11,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Complete the matching Icecrown Heroic meta, including healing, opposite vampire states and controlled plague stacks.\n\n1. Track Glory of the Icecrown Raider (25 player). Set the raid to 25-player Heroic before entering Icecrown Citadel (53.7, 87.0). Heroic wing completions are part of the meta, so a purely Normal clear will not finish it. Arrange a healer and damage control before the setup encounters.\n\n2. Marrowgar - Boned: kill quickly or free any impaled player within eight seconds. Deathwhisper - Full House: leave her mana barrier intact, let cultist waves spawn and transform, and keep five different required types alive together: Cult Fanatic, Deformed Fanatic, Reanimated Fanatic, Cult Adherent, and Reanimated Adherent. Only then break the shield and kill her with single-target damage; dismiss pets and avoid cleaves that would kill the adds.\n\n3. Gunship - I'm on a Boat: use the cannons, and keep every player's visits to the enemy ship to at most one. On a strong legacy clear, destroy it without boarding if possible. Saurfang - I've Gone and Made a Mess: defeat him before enough Marks of the Fallen Champion accumulate to fail the criterion.\n\n4. Plagueworks: kill Rotface before any Big Ooze casts Unstable Ooze Explosion; kill Festergut before anyone reaches three Inoculated stacks. At Putricide, never use the mutated abomination's Regurgitated Ooze slow; a quick kill avoids needing the vehicle. Complete the branch on Heroic.\n\n5. Blood Princes - The Orb Whisperer: kill the empowered prince quickly and avoid large empowered-orb hits on the group. Lana'thel - Once Bitten, Twice Shy: for one kill, body-pull, let combat register, and kill before receiving Essence of the Blood Queen. For the other, wait until that debuff actually appears, then kill her before its feeding/charm stage. Plan the second outcome on the same character after the weekly reset, in the same raid size.\n\n6. Valithria - Portal Jockey: heal her to full before any portals spawn. This satisfies the no-missed-portal condition and is much simpler than entering portals solo and resetting the encounter. If portals do spawn, every one must be used by the group before finishing. A healer is the reliable option; do not skip Valithria on this meta route.\n\n7. Sindragosa - All You Can Eat: kill quickly before anyone exceeds five Mystic Buffet stacks. If the fight lasts, use the ice tombs to reset stacks. Finish both Frostwing encounters on Heroic for the wing criterion.\n\n8. Lich King - Been Waiting a Long Time for This: remove attacking pets, damage auras, and automatic damage equipment. Start Tirion's dialogue, keep the boss in phase one without damaging him, and let him summon adds while Necrotic Plague jumps between them and you. The bottom throne steps can help your position, but actively avoid Shadow Traps and heal if needed; do not assume the staircase guarantees safety.\n\n9. Watch the actual Necrotic Plague stack count on yourself or the adds. It can disappear from your debuffs while on another target. Wait until one plague reaches at least 30 stacks, then finish the Lich King. Do not use his separate Plague Siphon buff as the counter. Wait through the scripted death, resurrection, and final kill before judging whether the achievement completed.\n\n10. For the 25-player meta, also complete Neck-Deep in Vile: kill every spawned Vile Spirit before it explodes, then defeat the Lich King. If your high-level kill skips their phase entirely, verify the awarded criterion after the ending.\n\n11. Return after reset for the opposite Lana'thel outcome and any failed boss conditions. Once all matching-size criteria and Heroic wings complete, check the mailbox for Reins of the Icebound Frostbrood Vanquisher and use them. The 10- and 25-player metas award different mounts and remain separate in Retail.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=51955",
        difficultyReason = "Complete the matching Icecrown Heroic meta, including healing, opposite vampire states and controlled plague stacks.",
        difficulty = "hard",
