        name = "Crimson Deathcharger",
        mountCategory = "Quest Rewards",
        stepCount = 11,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - The tradable reins can bypass Shadowmourne; the self-earned route needs helpers and weekly shard farming.\n\n1. Choose the purchase or quest route. Reins of the Crimson Deathcharger can be bought on the Auction House or traded by another player; if you buy the actual reins, use them directly and skip the legendary chain. This is different from the Death Knight's blue Acherus Deathcharger.\n\n2. For the quest route, use a Warrior, Paladin, or Death Knight and enter 25-player Icecrown Citadel (53.7, 87.0). Clear entrance trash to Friendly with the Ashen Verdict, then take The Sacred and the Corrupt from Highlord Darion Mograine on the left inside the entrance. Only the player completing the legendary needs this class restriction.\n\n3. With that quest active, visit Frostmourne Cavern in northeastern Dragonblight (74.4, 23.5). Interact with Light's Vengeance, wait through the Lich King's scene, use the hammer again as prompted, and defeat the resurrected enemy. Loot Light's Vengeance once the sequence finishes.\n\n4. Gather 25 Primordial Saronite and loot Rotface's Acidic Blood and Festergut's Acidic Blood from their 25-player kills. Bring all four components to Mograine's runeforge, complete the turn-ins, and obtain Shadow's Edge.\n\n5. For A Feast of Souls, equip Shadow's Edge and collect 50 souls from Icecrown enemies. Let Shadow's Fate apply before killing each target; instant kills can miss the credit. A Death Knight can use Chains of Ice to apply it without a damaging hit, and a Protection Warrior can use Demoralizing Shout. Watch the quest counter rather than killing an entire corridor before noticing zero progress.\n\n6. Unholy Infusion, 25-player Putricide: keep Shadow's Edge equipped and arrange a helper to hold the boss while you use the laboratory table to become an abomination. Let several slime puddles form, absorb them with the vehicle ability until you have 100 energy, then complete the Shadow Infusion cast. Only after the infusion buff is active should the group finish Putricide. Keep all damage controlled so the boss survives the setup.\n\n7. Blood Infusion, 25-player Lana'thel: with Shadow's Edge equipped, gain Blood Mirror and the initial vampire bite, then personally bite other players three times when Vampiric Bite becomes available. Bring enough helpers and coordinate their own feeding so nobody is mind-controlled before your third bite. Finish Lana'thel after the three bites; a quick ordinary kill does not complete this quest.\n\n8. Frost Infusion, 25-player Sindragosa: keep Shadow's Edge equipped, face the dragon, and survive four Frost Breaths before killing her. Hold damage and heal through the waiting period; do not one-shot her before the four-breath infusion is present.\n\n9. For The Splintered Throne, collect 50 Shadowfrost Shards from eligible 25-player boss kills over weekly lockouts. Finish forging Shadowmourne, take The Lich King's Last Stand, and kill the Lich King with the completed legendary equipped. Loot the Sealed Chest before leaving.\n\n10. Return the chest to Darion Mograine inside the raid and open the resulting reward container. Take Alexandros' Soul Shard to Darion for Mograine's Reunion; the reward is Reins of the Crimson Deathcharger. It is not a normal random mount roll from the Lich King.\n\n11. Use the reins to learn the mount, or keep them unlearned if intentionally trading them. Repeating weekly Lich King kills with the same completed Shadowmourne chain does not create a fresh chest each week.",
